  "methods": ["separation of variables", "integrating"],
  "statement": "Solve $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=2xy$, given that $y=3$ when $x=0$.",
  "solution": "Separating variables,\n$$\\frac{dy}{y}=2x\\,dx\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\ln|y|=x^2+C.$$\nSo $y=Ae^{x^2}$ for some constant $A$. Using $y(0)=3$ gives $A=3$. Hence\n$$y=3e^{x^2}.$$",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
  "hints": [
    "Separate: dy/y = 2x dx.",
    "Integrate both sides.",
    "Apply y(0)=3 to find A."
  ]
}
